---
import "../styles/global.css"
import Navigation from "../components/Navigation.astro"
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro"
import GtagHead from "../components/GtagHead.astro"
import NotifuseAnalytics from "../components/NotifuseAnalytics.astro"
import VerifyIcon from "../components/VerifyIcon.astro"
import CustomModal from "../components/CustomModal.astro"
import RegulatedCloud from "../components/RegulatedCloud.astro"
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <title>Regulated industries - Notifuse</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Email for regulated organisations, on infrastructure you already qualify: SSO, granular permissions, scoped API keys, audit logs, auditable code and no data leaving your perimeter. No certification is claimed for the software itself."
    />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://notifuse.com/regulated-industries" />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />
    <GtagHead />
    <NotifuseAnalytics />
  </head>

  <body class="bg-white-98 text-slate-900">
    <div class="container relative border-r border-l border-gray-200">
      <Navigation />

      <main>
        <section class="pt-20 pb-16 px-4 lg:px-8">
          <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-start">
            <div class="text-center lg:text-left">
              <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">
                Email on infrastructure you already qualify
              </h1>
              <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-8">
                For health, insurance, finance and other regulated organisations:
                deploy Notifuse inside the perimeter you already control, with the
                access controls and the audit trail your reviewers ask for.
              </p>
              <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 justify-center lg:justify-start">
                <a href="https://demo.notifuse.com/console/signin?email=demo@notifuse.com" class="bg-primary text-white px-6 py-2.5 rounded-md font-semibold hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors">See the live interface</a>
                <a href="/security" class="border border-gray-200 text-gray-700 px-6 py-2.5 rounded-md font-semibold hover:bg-white transition-colors">Read our security page</a>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="w-full max-w-[520px] mx-auto"><RegulatedCloud /></div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="py-16 px-4 lg:px-8 border-t border-gray-200">
          <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Why regulated organisations self-host</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
              A hosted marketing platform adds a sub-processor to your register:
              contact data, reading habits and campaign content sit on servers
              your organisation did not qualify, under contracts you cannot
              inspect at code level.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700">
              Self-hosted, the software runs where your other qualified systems
              already run. The database is yours, each workspace is isolated,
              and the code can be read by your own teams before it is deployed.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="py-16 px-4 lg:px-8 border-t border-gray-200">
          <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Health data: what certification does and does not cover</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
              In France, hosting personal health data requires an HDS-certified
              host. That certification attaches to the hosting provider and its
              perimeter — not to a piece of software.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
              <strong class="text-slate-900">Notifuse claims no HDS certification, and no
              certification is promised for the software itself.</strong>{" "}
              If your sending involves health data, deploy Notifuse on your own
              certified infrastructure, or with a host that holds the required
              certification for the data you process. Qualifying the deployment
              remains your organisation's responsibility, as it does for the
              rest of your stack.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700">
              The same logic applies in other regimes: we make no HIPAA, ISO
              27001 or other attestation claim for Notifuse. What we provide is
              software your organisation can qualify inside its own compliance
              perimeter — and keep email content free of medical information
              wherever a simple notification is enough.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="py-16 px-4 lg:px-8 border-t border-gray-200">
          <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">What your reviewers can verify</h2>
            <ul class="space-y-4 text-gray-700">
              <li class="flex gap-3"><VerifyIcon name="users" /><span><strong class="text-slate-900">Access control.</strong>{" "}Single sign-on through your identity provider, granular permissions per workspace, and scoped API keys.</span></li>
              <li class="flex gap-3"><VerifyIcon name="book" /><span><strong class="text-slate-900">Audit logs.</strong>{" "}Admin actions are recorded, so who changed what — templates, settings, permissions — can be reviewed after the fact.</span></li>
              <li class="flex gap-3"><VerifyIcon name="code" /><span><strong class="text-slate-900">The code.</strong>{" "}The source is public, and each release becomes AGPL-3.0 after four years. Your teams can read what they deploy.</span></li>
              <li class="flex gap-3"><VerifyIcon name="shield" /><span><strong class="text-slate-900">The security process.</strong>{" "}Private vulnerability reports, a reply within three business days, first assessment within ten, fixes in the latest release with a public advisory. Details on our{" "}<a href="/security" class="text-primary hover:underline">security page</a>.</span></li>
              <li class="flex gap-3"><VerifyIcon name="wifi-off" /><span><strong class="text-slate-900">No phone-home.</strong>{" "}Licence keys are checked locally. Nothing about your installation is sent to us.</span></li>
              <li class="flex gap-3"><VerifyIcon name="licence" /><span><strong class="text-slate-900">The licence.</strong>{" "}What needs a key, what never will, and what happens without one — written, dated and versioned on our{" "}<a href="/pricing/self-hosted" class="text-primary hover:underline">licence page</a>.</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="py-16 px-4 lg:px-8 border-t border-gray-200">
          <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">An example</h2>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-3">Illustrative scenario — not a customer case.</p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
              A group of clinics deploys Notifuse on the group's certified
              hosting. Each clinic has its own workspace, contacts and domain;
              appointment reminders carry no medical content, only a time and a
              link to the patient portal. Staff sign in through the group's
              identity provider, and admin actions stay in the audit logs for
              the compliance team to review.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700">
              When the group adds entities, it moves to a Custom licence rather
              than changing tools.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="py-16 px-4 lg:px-8 border-t border-gray-200">
          <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">How purchasing works</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
              Standard licences are bought online. Larger deployments — several
              entities, more than fifteen workspaces, specific requirements — use a
              {" "}<a href="/pricing/self-hosted#custom" class="text-primary hover:underline">Custom licence</a>:
              quoted per deployment, with purchase-order purchasing. Paid licences
              include private email support in English and French, Monday to Friday.
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
              <a href="/pricing/self-hosted" class="bg-primary text-white px-6 py-2.5 rounded-md font-semibold hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors">Compare licences</a>
              <button type="button" data-custom-open class="border border-gray-200 text-gray-700 px-6 py-2.5 rounded-md font-semibold hover:bg-white transition-colors">Talk about a Custom licence</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </main>

      <CustomModal />
      <Footer />
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
